# Topic: Chess
T:Chess
T:Reference
T:Category
T:Arts
T:------------
T:What it is
T:Chess is a
T:board game
T:for two
T:players,
T:played on a
T:square board
T:consisting
T:of 64
T:squares
T:arranged in
T:an 8×8 grid.
T:The players,
T:referred to
T:as "White"
T:and "Black",
T:each control
T:sixteen
T:pieces: one
T:king, one
T:queen, two
T:rooks, two
T:bishops, two
T:knights, and
T:eight pawns,
T:with each
T:piece type
T:having a
T:different
T:pattern of
T:movement. An
T:enemy piece
T:may be
T:captured by
T:moving one's
T:own piece
T:onto the
T:square it
T:occupies.
T:The
T:objective of
T:the game is
T:to checkmate
T:the enemy
T:king. There
T:are also
T:several ways
T:a game can
T:end in a
T:draw.
